{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label","id":780907,"title":"Wyrm taint used as a label","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T21:39:08-08:00","id":780907,"title":"Wyrm taint used as a label","content":"has anyone else felt that Wyrm taint has been used as a label for something an author or ST Thinks is bad, reflecting their politics, or philosophical views?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:03:47-08:00","id":780917,"title":"","content":"No, what ever would draw you to that conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:19:36-08:00","id":780928,"title":"","content":"I can't tell if Dwight is being sarcastic.<br /> <br /> I definitely feel Werewolf has a strong left wing bias, and especially in first edition there is a sense that Wyrm taint is anything double unplus good. Whether that shows up in any chronicle depends on the ST though.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be that way though.<br /> <br /> In my games, I only apply Wyrm taint to things that are either &quot;unnatural&quot;, supernatural evil, or intrinsically unhealthy to Gaian life (Earth's biosphere) - that includes radiation, cancer, toxic chemicals, any number of carcinogens, etc. I shy away from anything that makes it look like a particular political ideology is &quot;tainted&quot; - although I have no problem showing particular individuals in any political tradition being of the Wyrm provided they engage in obvious evil.<br /> <br /> I use Wyrm taint as a kind of spiritual pollution or miasma, so people can show taint who aren't evil themselves simply because they are exposed to it.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I use it as a way to prod PCs to investigate story hooks, not as a &quot;detect evil&quot; that doesn't need the players to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:14:31-08:00","id":781120,"title":"","content":"Yep, seen that through ooc debates. I've also seen players forget it's not set in the real world, it's set in the World of Darkness. A fictitious place where the Wyrm does hide and sneak in to undemine, pervert, defile politics and philosophical views in subtle manipulations to twist those ideals and comforts of acceptance and personal views we in real life hold to.<br /> <br /> Thing is, both types of people need to remember its a fictitious piece. That no one is saying in real life tjose things are Tainted. Only in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> it is afterall a game for mature minds who hopefully can separate the two and if something does trigger a personal response to be able to be in a safe ebvironment to be able to gain the clarity with others before proceeding onwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:37:05-08:00","id":781254,"title":"","content":"how bad do you think it would be for an ST to make that kind of ruling in a game. Think its more likely to keep things fresh or to seem arbitrary","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:18:02-08:00","id":781340,"title":"","content":"It depends too much on the group, ST and players, because it depends on your view of the game and also in your ideologies, shared and, specially, not shared. If you all strongly agree that a given idea is evil, who am I to go against you making it Wyrm-Tainted in your game? But for me, as an example, even the ideas I'm strongly against shouldn't be instantly Wyrm-Tainted, because I like to make ideological differences a thing in my games.<br /> <br /> What you have to be aware, aside tastes among your troupe (that you should to be aware anyway), is ideological <u>differences</u> between you. No matter how much you thing idea X is wrong, someone, maybe someone you don't expect, will think it right. And maybe you'll hurt this person if you present her idea as Wyrm-Tainted.<br /> <br /> An RPG is the perfect place for the ST to make every political view it wants completely correct. That can be incredible disgusting for players who don't share this view. DON'T use this to market your ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:12:41-08:00","id":781369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=781340#post781340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An RPG is the perfect place for the ST to make every political view it wants completely correct. That can be incredible disgusting for players who don't share this view. DON'T use this to market your ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? I mean look at how the CoG book did it, look how that turned out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:30:01-08:00","id":781377,"title":"","content":"allready had someone I ranted about once or twice before tried introducing to WTA a decade ago or so and she threatened to quit without OUTRAGEOUS Changes... including ... making albrecht a pawn of the CIA HAve the government have in depth files on the garou nation and camarilla<br /> <br /> And Make the umbra an &quot;Alternate dimsension the government is using for Nuclear weapons testing&quot; Because she disliked things like strip mining nuclear weapons testing etc Leaving EVIL Spiritual consequences...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:53:48-08:00","id":781387,"title":"","content":"I had a person in a VTT game on AOL I may have ranted about a time or two before who couldnt handle the &quot;Portraying modern American liberal views as gospel&quot; thats canon in the game<br /> <br /> then she SUCKED me into a shittiy D&amp;D game everyone but me had a fun time which even made it worse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:57:06-08:00","id":781389,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know the story, and it is indeed a good example. Your friend couldn't stomach Werewolf precisely because the game makes a lot of political assumptions that were against her beliefs. This is the problem with the game, and I admit it even being mostly politically aligned with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:14:37-08:00","id":781402,"title":"","content":"Dont think of her as a Friend anymore... look when your Relationship with someone REVOLVES around gaming, breaking it off because of such problems is reasonable...<br /> <br /> those who arent opposed to these beliefs can revel in it though... and I think Excising it would do more harm then good... though I'd like the enemys to be more &quot;Progress &quot; and (in their minds) &quot;Helping humanity&quot; and less &quot;GLORY TO DECAY!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 12-06-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T04:57:31-08:00","id":781657,"title":"","content":"Well... &quot;Wyrm-tainted&quot; is a laber strongly radicated in Werewolf, and is mostly used for badmouthing others...<br /> -Europeans Garou are &quot;wyrm-bringers&quot;,<br /> -the Gnawers are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they live in the slums (kalokagathia)<br /> -the Glass Walkers, when non &quot;weaver tainted&quot; are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; (someone don't see the difference)<br /> -the Shadow Lords are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; even though they were the one that stood against the Darkness in Transylvania<br /> -the Silver Fang are inbred &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; even though they are the one that stood against the Darkness in Russia (you can see the dycothomy with the Lords)<br /> -the Silent Striders are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they don't run in packs<br /> -the Uktena are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they dabble in strange secrets<br /> -the Black Furies are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they hate men<br /> -the Get of Fenris are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they are eugenethic machos (oversemplification)<br /> -the Red Talons are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they hate (and ate) humans<br /> -the Wendigo are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they hate europeans (both humans and supernaturals)<br /> -the Fianna are &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; because they are an alcoholic bunch dabbling in human politic and with common ancestors with the Spirals<br /> -the Children of Gaia may not be tainted but are a bunch of weakling<br /> <br /> and why the Stargazers should go and leave the Garou Nation? Surely they got something to hide, are they perhaps tainted, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 12-07-2015, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:08:27-08:00","id":781689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=780928#post780928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, I only apply Wyrm taint to things that are either &quot;unnatural&quot;, supernatural evil, or intrinsically unhealthy to Gaian life (Earth's biosphere) - that includes radiation, cancer, toxic chemicals, any number of carcinogens, etc. I shy away from anything that makes it look like a particular political ideology is &quot;tainted&quot; - although I have no problem showing particular individuals in any political tradition being of the Wyrm provided they engage in obvious evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found this list a bit odd, since if you take a look at what's going on near Chernobyl, you'll see that hard radiation is less toxic to the environment than civilization.<br /> <br /> Also the game paints BDSM as being thoroughly wyrm-tainted, so it's clearly not just left wing good, right wing bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:26:23-08:00","id":781702,"title":"","content":"oh remember glancing throuhg original &quot;hunters hunted&quot;<br /> <br /> Saw a reference to its leadership hoping to use Vampires as a weapon to those against &quot;Red blooded americans&quot; Including roleplayers, back to nature people, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:53:26-08:00","id":781830,"title":"","content":"Radiation cannot be inherently Wyrmish, as just living would cover everyone in more Wyrm then exists in the setting. I think that people are mixing up author soapboxes on how nasty Right Wing things are with what is actually of the Wyrm. I've always found it hilarious how right wing the Shifters are compared to the general message the game is trying to convey.<br /> <br /> Republicans and Shia are not inherently of the Wyrm. Liberals can also serve the Wyrm and its purposes. This is something has been conveyed quite clearly by the game even while it passed all the judgment for the carelessness of the (quite specifically) rightwing Americans. The game could have always used a more in depth look at practical politics beyond the borders of the USA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:49:22-08:00","id":781850,"title":"","content":"I remember the revised Strider book probably had the closest thing to a right wing message that I can remember when they did a little bit about the spirit world inside abortion clinics. I'll admit I was surprised to see them paint abortion clinics in possibly not such a positive light after the CoG book had a little aside about reproductive rights. Granted the Strider book did have a &quot;we have no position on abortion&quot; disclaimer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:01:50-08:00","id":782044,"title":"","content":"I don't care what your politics are, abortion clinics can be fucking gross places; front might be nice but the back is... less than pleasant, what with all that 'medical waste.' Kermit Gosnell's case might be a good example of a some of the things that would attract banes in particular. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=781830#post781830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiation cannot be inherently Wyrmish, as just living would cover everyone in more Wyrm then exists in the setting. I think that people are mixing up author soapboxes on how nasty Right Wing things are with what is actually of the Wyrm. I've always found it hilarious how right wing the Shifters are compared to the general message the game is trying to convey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno; the Garou might be conservative, in that they resist change to their society, but they are not really 'right wing' in a political sense at all. The Garou Nation does not support any of the 'pro-gun, pro-corporation, small government, few taxes' platforms associated with the American right wing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:48:16-08:00","id":782172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=782044#post782044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno; the Garou might be conservative, in that they resist change to their society, but they are not really 'right wing' in a political sense at all. The Garou Nation does not support any of the 'pro-gun, pro-corporation, small government, few taxes' platforms associated with the American right wing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I referred to the fact that the game is stuck in the American political views. Right wing also covers conservatism, family values, religion and a number of other things near and dear to the Garou nation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T10:14:51-08:00","id":786063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=781689#post781689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the game paints BDSM as being thoroughly wyrm-tainted, so it's clearly not just left wing good, right wing bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say BDSM is Weaver-ish, if anything... :&gt; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T21:29:13-08:00","id":790083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=782044#post782044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care what your politics are, abortion clinics can be fucking gross places; front might be nice but the back is... less than pleasant, what with all that 'medical waste.' Kermit Gosnell's case might be a good example of a some of the things that would attract banes in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. That wasn't your typical c!inic. That was the den of a monster who preyed on desperate women to make a profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T23:23:06-08:00","id":790117,"title":"","content":"All those bits, brains and limbs and placenta have to go somewhere...<i> or feed something</i>. The grist produced by plastic surgery mills is similarly foul. Different sort of clientele, different problems of the heart, but I am sure the Wyrm can and will do its work in either place.<br /> <br /> It does not have to be that way, but the potential for a story is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:58:25-08:00","id":790352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> has anyone else felt that Wyrm taint has been used as a label for something an author or ST Thinks is bad, reflecting their politics, or philosophical views? </div> </div> </div>I got that sense very quickly when reading my first werewolf book, the revised core. I made the decision then to divorce my understanding of reality from anything in werewolf if that's the game I'm running and treat everything through the lens of the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> For example, in real life, there's lots of companies, big and small, that have a benevolent corporate culture and generally take care of their employees. In the World of Darkness that I run, that kind of corporate culture is a myth, propagated by those fools desperate for hope.<br /> <br /> Or take Law Enforcement. Most of those people are generally decent folks. But in my World of Darkness, more often than not they are on some kind of a power trip backed up with a system of corruption and your rights are a formality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8365-pensman","name":"Pensman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8365_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:56:22-07:00","id":919355,"title":"","content":"Thought I'd bump this thread rather then create another one.<br /> <br /> in a Pre Abolition America.<br /> <br /> or in Rome in a White Howler game, or in a Dark Ages game, or in colonial times or whatever.<br /> <br /> is it beyond the realm of reason for a Non BSD garou to own slaves?<br /> <br /> Its easy to argue that the Treatment of slaves could create wyrm taint, but same argument works for treatment of kin and Metis.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or in Modern times as a Slum Lord or Drug Dealer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-22-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T18:22:42-07:00","id":919425,"title":"","content":"Slavery was a universal human institution found in all cultures. Even societies that lacked large scale slavery on plantations, mines, and other dehumanizing conditions would have household slaves in the family doing hard and dreary work.<br /> <br /> So I don't think slavery in and of itself would register as Wyrm tainted. Depending on how you interpret Wyrm taint, it might show up in certain treatment of slaves, but that would be true of treatment of non-slaves as well.<br /> <br /> One can argue that the Garou's treatment of kinfolk is essentially a master-slave relationship, although this is less true now than in the past. Most likely any slaves a Garou would own would be through their kinfolk, not directly.<br /> <br /> As for slum lords and drug dealers, again it depends on how you interpret Wyrm taint. However, any situation which would attract Banes in large numbers to a small geographic area is likely going to cause that area to register Wyrm taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:00:33-07:00","id":919525,"title":"","content":"The only time i felt that way was with reading rage across the amazon. It did kind of have a leftist &quot;Trees good, man bad&quot; feel...<br /> BUT then i loved Rage across russia where it showed a # of natural &amp; man made disasters in the REAL world that dwarf some of what is seen in the WoD..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:48:31-07:00","id":919545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=919425#post919425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slavery was a universal human institution found in all cultures. Even societies that lacked large scale slavery on plantations, mines, and other dehumanizing conditions would have household slaves in the family doing hard and dreary work.<br /> <br /> So I don't think slavery in and of itself would register as Wyrm tainted. Depending on how you interpret Wyrm taint, it might show up in certain treatment of slaves, but that would be true of treatment of non-slaves as well.<br /> <br /> One can argue that the Garou's treatment of kinfolk is essentially a master-slave relationship, although this is less true now than in the past. Most likely any slaves a Garou would own would be through their kinfolk, not directly.<br /> <br /> As for slum lords and drug dealers, again it depends on how you interpret Wyrm taint. <b>However, any situation which would attract Banes in large numbers to a small geographic area is likely going to cause that area to register Wyrm taint.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Like slavery, for example. This could be seen as a kind of indictment of much of human society, which is a thing that Werewolf does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:10:32-07:00","id":919754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=919545#post919545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like slavery, for example. This could be seen as a kind of indictment of much of human society, which is a thing that Werewolf does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Banes being attracted to a large plantation where many slaves were brutally mistreated. <br /> <br /> But's let's say a homestead closer to the Appalachians were there is a single slave who is treated more like a part of the family - I don't see Banes going there any more than I see Banes going to a Norse family's farm that had a single thrall in the same way. Or perhaps a family in ancient Rome who own slaves in their home who fill the roles of domestic servants, tutors for their children, and perhaps other highly skilled professions who stand a good chance of being manumitted before they die. I don't see Banes there. Although the same family might own a mine or quarry where many slaves toil and have a high mortality rate, and I'd expect Banes to be there. But in all these cases, it would not be the institution of slavery per se - but the actual treatment of people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:23:37-07:00","id":919761,"title":"","content":"A good point, though one thing, where this gets problematic, how were the garou able to justify the impergium then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:07:42-07:00","id":919784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=919761#post919761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good point, though one thing, where this gets problematic, how were the garou able to justify the impergium then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean to themselves, or in some kind of objective sense? Because in the latter capacity, it won't work unless the Garou were supporting the Ratkin, whose duty it is to keep human numbers low. In the former case, it's because they WERE CLEARLY GAIA'S CHOSEN, SET ABOVE ALL OTHERS AS WARRIORS SUPREME!<br /> <br /> Also, that was around ten thousand years ago, and a lot of modern Garou either don't try to justify it, being homid, or are part of a tiny minority that didn't think that it went far enough, and would have preferred to have just ended humans outright..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:24:03-07:00","id":919861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=