ate:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:03:41-07:00","id":986139,"title":"","content":"Its interesting how this thread resurrected.<br /> <br /> Well, I would say that the possibility of a Fetish for Kin, as any way to reveal or hide Wyrm-Taint, should work on a chronicle-necessity basis. I'm currently running a chronicle where a fetish was designed to hide Wyrm-Taint, in a breackthrough so outstanding that it is almost mass-producted, and so perfect that very, very few ways exist to bypass it. The main one is to use a Gift of at least level 2 to detect the taint while inside a place equivalent to a level 5 Caern especifically blessed by a thruth-revealing spirit. It isn't quite easy.<br /> <br /> But why all that? Well, because the chronicle revolves around confusion, betrayal of the two sides, hard questions with hard decisions, and the world going to hell whyle the PCs need to decide the best way to deal with the Apocalypse itself removing the greatest weapon of the Nation: a clear enemy.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's just one of infinite ways to do that. I do think it quite reasonable to have a relatively common fetish to detect Wyrm-Taint. What you should think first is what effect you want on your chronicle. Even if everyone have a natural level of Wyrm-Taint, maybe it isn't hard to determine some degrees of such Taint after some training: there is a range where it is certainly only the natural trace, there is a range where it is obviously a serious touch of the Wyrm, and there is a range where the doubt stays, but then you know you need to keep an eye. Are great levels of Taint only possible for things really devoted to the enemy in your chronicle? Then only the naive should mistake what to do. The presence of the Wyrm is only a first sign? So it is quite a conundrum to decide what to do. Does the Garou Nation and the Kin disagree on that matter? Sometimes different people with the same devotion would just see some aspects differently and so take distinct decisions.<br /> <br /> A doctor, or police officer, that depares with such taint, well. Actually any reaction would be valid I do think it reasonable for a Kin to decide that medicine provided by the Wyrm, if not actualy Tainted itself, should first be used for some good. And maybe even if Tainted, if she thinks it wouldn't cause much harm by itself. The consequences of such decisions, though, depend on what Wyrm-Taint means in your chronicle, and how it is measured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:13:58-07:00","id":986144,"title":"","content":"The Rite of the Morning Song pretty much trumps the need for such a fetish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:45:54-07:00","id":986159,"title":"","content":"Where do I find this rite? Confess I never heard of, but I'm not a savant on rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:51:41-07:00","id":986162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=919784#post919784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean to themselves, or in some kind of objective sense? Because in the latter capacity, it won't work unless the Garou were supporting the Ratkin, whose duty it is to keep human numbers low. In the former case, it's because they WERE CLEARLY GAIA'S CHOSEN, SET ABOVE ALL OTHERS AS WARRIORS SUPREME!<br /> <br /> Also, that was around ten thousand years ago, and a lot of modern Garou either don't try to justify it, being homid, or are part of a tiny minority that didn't think that it went far enough, and would have preferred to have just ended humans outright..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the Record, yes I meant to themselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:58:07-07:00","id":986165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=986159#post986159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do I find this rite? Confess I never heard of, but I'm not a savant on rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Kinfolk a Breed Apart.<br /> <br /> YAY Kinfolk have rites now.<br /> <br /> good or bad, at least it helps to close the power differential between Kinfolk and ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:42:03-07:00","id":986394,"title":"","content":"I am not sure why people keep saying that Kinfolk with Gifts are rare. In Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, it just says that Kinfolk with multiple gifts are uncommon and that it was up to the ST whether to allow any PC to learn Gifts (as in, before you agree to play a Kinfolk, make sure that your ST will allow you to purchase Gifts during play if you really want to purchase Gifts during play). Now, Kinfolk with Gnosis are rare, but rare events are generally considered to have an odds of 1:2,500 or less, so is it rare compared to the Kinfolk population or the Human population?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:21:38-07:00","id":986459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=986394#post986394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure why people keep saying that Kinfolk with Gifts are rare. In Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, it just says that Kinfolk with multiple gifts are uncommon and that it was up to the ST whether to allow any PC to learn Gifts (as in, before you agree to play a Kinfolk, make sure that your ST will allow you to purchase Gifts during play if you really want to purchase Gifts during play). Now, Kinfolk with Gnosis are rare, but rare events are generally considered to have an odds of 1:2,500 or less, so is it rare compared to the Kinfolk population or the Human population?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do kinfolk learn their gifts from spirits? because if so then not having Gnosis is gonna be a pretty big issue there.<br /> <br /> Also I'd imagine that the 1:2500 would be amongst the kinfolk population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T18:01:17-07:00","id":986498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/780907-wyrm-taint-used-as-a-label?p=986394#post986394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure why people keep saying that Kinfolk with Gifts are rare. In Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, it just says that Kinfolk with multiple gifts are uncommon</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, Pg. 54</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many might a mere kinfolk possess? Perhaps one, if he's lucky, maybe two if he's incredibly talented and worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps one, <u>if he's lucky</u> does not imply common to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 Kinfolk: A Breed Apart, Pg. 64-65</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, the number of Gifts a Kinfolk may possess should never outstrip what would be reasonable for a Garou. A Kinfolk character with more than two or three Gifts would have to have very good reasons for possessing so many! Most Kinfolk who can use Gifts have one Gift; occasionally, a talented and Gaia-blessed Kinfolk might have two Gifts. Under very special circumstances, and only as a reward for exceptional roleplaying, a Kinfolk who accomplished something unique and epic, might acquire three Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording certainly seems to imply that Kinfolk with Gifts are in fact rare (again, be nitpicky about the use of the term &quot;rare&quot; if you want). Admittedly, as of W20, they seem <i>more</i> common. But even then, I would say far from every kinfolk should have (even access to) them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T18:29:57-07:00","id":986505,"title":"","content":"Oh the comment on Spanking, comes from Page 83, from Freak legion, as for opposition to violence on television, the entirety, of Action bill seems to be a statement about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}